  "notes": "Composed of {対|たい} (facing, opposing) + {談|だん} (talk). Specifically refers to a two-person conversation, often in a published or broadcast format. Used as both a noun and a する verb.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {対談|たいだん}する: to have a dialogue\n- {対談|たいだん}{記事|きじ}: dialogue article; published conversation\n- {対談|たいだん}{番組|ばんぐみ}: talk show (dialogue format)\n- {対談|たいだん}{集|しゅう}: collection of dialogues\n- {対談|たいだん}{相手|あいて}: dialogue partner\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {会話|かいわ}: everyday conversation (informal, any number of people)\n- {鼎談|ていだん}: three-person discussion (rare, literary)\n- {座談|ざだん}: roundtable talk (more than two people, informal setting)\n- インタビュー: interview (one person asks, one answers — less equal than {対談|たいだん})",
